# What does NOT get uploaded to the deployment.
#
# Root Directory is "." and vercel.json declares no exclusions, so without this
# file EVERY file in the repo is fetchable at https://www.brandmintstudios.in/.
# That is how /PLAN.md, /CLAUDE.md and /brand-mint-admin/ came to be public.
#
# Nothing below is referenced by any served page — checked before excluding.
# This changes what is *published*, not what is in git.

# ── commercially sensitive ─────────────────────────────────────
# PLAN.md and docs/STUDIO-FACTS.md carry real cash MRR, the break-even gap,
# named clients and which of them has not paid. brand-mint-admin/ holds
# contract templates and a P&L. None of it belongs on a public host.
PLAN.md
docs/
brand-mint-admin/

# ── tells an attacker where to look ────────────────────────────
# CLAUDE.md names the admin account, the Firebase project, and states plainly
# that tenant isolation is unproven. firestore.rules is the security boundary
# in full. Neither is a secret — the rules are enforced server-side and
# obscurity is not a control — but there is no reason to hand over the map.
CLAUDE.md
firestore.rules
firebase.json

# ── the legacy CRM, taken off the public host ──────────────────
# admin.html served at /admin with NO authentication. Lines 29-38 of that file
# write a 365-day session token on load for the stated purpose of bypassing the
# gate, and `noindex` keeps it out of Google without stopping anyone who types
# the URL.
#
# Its Supabase project is not in the account any more, so it falls back to the
# seed in admin/db.js — which sets a legal entity name, gstin 36ABCDE1234F1Z5
# (36 is Telangana's real GST state code, and the string is correctly formed),
# a PAN, and an HDFC account and IFSC. admin/modules/invoices.js prints the
# GSTIN and the IFSC onto generated invoices.
#
# So the URL let anyone produce a document that looks like a Brand Mint tax
# invoice carrying a plausible fake GSTIN and bank account. No client data was
# exposed — all of it is fabricated — which is exactly what makes it bad
# rather than harmless (§4: a plausible-looking tax number on an invoice is not
# a placeholder, it is a false statement).
#
# /studio replaces everything this did and has real authentication. Excluded
# rather than deleted: every file stays in git and on the branch, untouched, so
# §5's do-not-touch still holds for the source and restoring is one line. This
# changes what is PUBLISHED, not what exists.
#
# Checked before excluding: nothing served references /admin — the only inbound
# links are admin.html's own stylesheet and module.
admin.html
admin/

# ── internal notes, no public value ────────────────────────────
BUILD-PLAYBOOK.md
COMPONENTS.md
REPO-INFO.md
README.md

# ── tooling: 6.5 MB of agent personas and design data ──────────
# Would otherwise be uploaded and served on every deploy.
.claude/
tests/
tools/
.gstack/

# ── never ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
*adminsdk*.json
*service-account*.json
node_modules/
